  "term": "Purdue Pegboard Test",
  "definition": "The Purdue Pegboard Test is a commonly used task for measuring manual dexterity, or how well a person coordinates hand movements with vision. In the supplied source, it is described as a general rather than dentistry-specific dexterity test, and it did not significantly predict students’ preclinical dental performance.",
